From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: athexweb3 <athexweb3@nirapod.org>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:08:32 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] Do not assume that system calls preserve the vector registers

A system call was assumed to preserve every callee-saved register in
full. Under -call-conv windows that includes xmm6-xmm15, but a Jasmin
xreg is the 256-bit ymm and the Microsoft x64 ABI only keeps its low
128 bits. AAPCS64 has the same gap for v8-v15 (low 64 bits only).

A calling convention now lists the registers a system call preserves
(syscall_preserved), a subset of callee_saved. Only Windows x64 leaves
registers out (xmm6-xmm15). There, an export that issues a syscall now
saves ymm6-ymm15, and a vector value live across a syscall has to be
spilled.
